WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:05.580
In May 2019, a small
counter narcotics unit

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.270
was rolling down a country road

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:10.010
in a rural part of Sinaloa,

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:13.420
which was the center of
the global drug empire

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:15.513
created by El Chapo Guzmán.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.740
They were overcome by a
pretty powerful smell.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.380
They were literally
stopped in their tracks

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:22.690
and it's one of the things

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:25.720
that people on these
counter-narcotics squads

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.270
are looking out, for smelling
out for in this case.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:31.470
So they got out of their vehicles

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:36.470
and through a clearing of
trees, they found five cauldrons

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.190
that were being used to produce heroin

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:41.820
and they also found four jugs

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:45.250
of a chemical called acetic
anhydride that was made

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:48.550
by a major multi-billion
dollar American company.

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:52.260
And the product brand was J.T. Baker.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.990
And that chemical is the only thing

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:57.770
other than the sap from opium flowers

00:00:57.770 --> 00:00:59.830
that you need to manufacture heroin

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:01.520
and under international drug laws,

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:03.080
it's one of the most highly controlled

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:07.123
of these chemicals sold anywhere
in the world, except Mexico.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.410
The great tragedy for
me in investigating this

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:16.070
was the idea that any American company

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:19.633
could be involved in that
even if it's unknowing.

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:24.580
It really made us feel like we
had to do everything we could

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:27.223
to expose this situation
and make it public.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.340
In the 1980s, there was a
flood of cocaine production

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:46.500
from Latin America into the United States.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:50.040
An epidemic of crack in New
York is now out of control.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.860
And there was a huge surge
in the use of cocaine

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.220
and then crack cocaine.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:57.150
Do you have no words to
describe how bad it is?

00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:00.720
I've seen young mothers
with babies and strollers

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.225
and small toddlers at their
skirt tail buying crack

00:02:04.225 --> 00:02:05.898
in the neighborhood where I live.

00:02:05.898 --> 00:02:08.470
Amidst sort of like a lot of concern

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:10.350
and even some hysteria
in the United States

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:11.560
about the cocaine problem

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:15.230
the CIA and the Drug Enforcement
Administration in the U.S.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:17.090
made a rather embarrassing discovery

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:19.540
that about 95% of the chemicals

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:23.640
that were used to make cocaine
in South America for the U.S.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:26.670
all came from American chemical companies.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:29.890
Behind closed doors at Senate
offices on Capitol Hill

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:31.280
the Senate Intelligence Committee

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:33.420
began its investigation this morning

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:36.190
one of several committees that
want to carry out hearings.

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:38.170
In Congress, there was a scandal

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:40.330
and there was a pretty swift reaction.

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:43.800
And so there were significant
amendments to the drug laws

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:47.470
requiring chemical companies
to take responsibility

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:50.120
for their sales overseas

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:53.730
and to make sure that from start to finish

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:57.490
the supply of drug making
chemicals went to customers

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:59.540
who had a legitimate purpose to use them

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:02.163
and weren't diverted to the drug trade.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:08.880
The U.S. aggressively pushed
international drug laws

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:09.713
around the world

00:03:09.713 --> 00:03:13.270
and virtually every country
has adopted domestic

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:17.000
and international controls
over these very same chemicals.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.240
There's a list called the Red List

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:22.090
and that list contains the chemicals

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:23.230
that are of the most concern

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:25.610
and they are the most highly regulated.

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:27.500
At the very top, the chemical

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:29.910
that is of the most
concern internationally

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:34.820
and has been since 2001, is a
chemical called acetic anhydride

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:37.990
and it is the only
critical essential chemical

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:39.980
that you need to make heroin

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:43.240
and that's why it's
number one on the Red List

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:47.140
and it's number one, under
international narcotics laws.

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:50.830
We were trying to figure out
knowing that acetic anhydride

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.990
was absolutely necessary for making heroin

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:54.550
and it was strictly controlled

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:57.648
how the drug cartels were
getting access to it.

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:08.110
Internationally, acetic
anhydride is heavily regulated.

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:12.460
For 18 years, Mexico avoided
stringent regulations.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:14.860
You know, they said that it
was too costly for companies,

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:15.856
it wasn't necessary.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:18.940
In 2018, they tightened the regulations.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:20.780
But even with those tighter regulations

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:23.870
we saw that sale of quantities

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:26.740
that should have been
regulated, went, you know

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:29.240
fell through the cracks,
went completely unnoticed.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:33.580
Regions where a lot of poppies being grown

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:37.090
farmers have to resort
to growing the plant

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:38.550
mainly because of poverty.

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:41.780
You know, they're not either
able to sustain their families

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:45.080
with the usual corn or bean crops

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:48.210
or they actually sometimes get threatened

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:50.120
by cartel groups that require

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:52.190
that they grow them on their plots.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:57.380
Mexico production of
heroin waxes and wanes

00:04:57.380 --> 00:05:01.020
but at its height, there is a huge demand

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:03.970
from the cartels for acetic anhydride

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:06.720
because that's really the only
ingredient missing for them.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:10.210
They have the farmers
producing their poppy for them.

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:15.210
So they just need to get
ahold of some jugs of the chemical

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:16.606
and then they're ready to go.

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:21.340
These chemical labs all
over poppy producing regions,

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:23.750
some of them get seized by the government

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:25.950
and then the government
snaps photos of them

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:26.910
sends them to the media,

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:28.940
the media puts them up on their websites

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:30.490
and with a simple Google search

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:33.370
you can see what these labs look like.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:36.460
So I'm scouring Google,
looking for chemical labs

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:41.380
and busts by the army
and I see a bunch of them

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:44.710
and they normally have a
lot of unmarked blue barrels

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:47.160
or unmarked bottles of chemicals.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:49.280
But I came upon one photo
where I actually saw

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:52.420
there was a label and the
label read "JT Baker".

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:55.140
I went through more searches
and I saw it in another photo

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:59.870
and JT Baker just kept popping
up as one of the only labels

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:01.898
that you could actually
see on the chemical

00:06:01.898 --> 00:06:02.648
in these lab busts.

00:06:02.648 --> 00:06:04.690
So we realized, okay,
something's happening here.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:09.320
So, JT Baker was a
century old American brand

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:13.190
that had this really
good worldwide reputation

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:17.420
for its purity and its purity
and control of its production

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:22.400
was a huge part of its marketing
to chemist at universities

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.850
to chemist in the
pharmaceutical industry

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:28.250
who use it in R and D,
research and development labs.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:31.970
It had been bought, the
brand, in August of 2010

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:35.200
by a company that became known as Avantor.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:37.210
From discovery to delivery

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:40.140
scientists and research
professionals worldwide

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:41.273
trust Avantor.

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:43.850
They really had a strong presence

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:45.950
in the lab chemical market worldwide

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:48.150
but especially in the Americas.

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:51.400
Their operation in Mexico
was a significant player

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:52.833
for them in the industry.

00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:01.810
So as we started looking
into this JT Baker brand

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:06.106
we started discovering a lot
of really extraordinary things.

00:07:06.565 --> 00:07:10.690
Sellers and distributors
in Mexico that we spoke to

00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:14.420
told us that it was incredibly
popular with the Narcos

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:15.730
and the reason it was so popular

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:16.990
was because for the same reason

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:19.400
that it was marketed for laboratories

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:22.073
was its purity and its
reputation for purity.

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:27.730
We found that the company was selling it

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:30.370
in these rather extraordinary containers.

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:32.700
So there are 20 liter size containers

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:36.820
which is it's a pretty substantial
black plastic container

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:37.981
to keep the sunlight out.

00:07:39.190 --> 00:07:42.400
Avantor had said that
this specific container

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:44.480
was the largest amount of chemical

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:46.640
you could get in a container designed

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:49.940
for a single operator to be
able to still use handily.

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:53.640
Now, the Narcos absolutely
loved these jugs.

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:58.050
They were perfect for the cottage
industry nature production

00:07:58.050 --> 00:07:59.433
of heroin in Mexico.

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:05.190
So, one thing we found
once we sort of studied

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:07.650
the market in Mexico and studied Avantor

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:09.580
was that Avantor distributes in Mexico

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:11.160
through what are called channel partners

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:13.350
which are essentially distributors.

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:17.030
And by law, they're only
supposed to sell acetic anhydride

00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:19.231
to legitimate users.

00:08:20.159 --> 00:08:23.770
I started going down the
list of the channel partners

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:26.730
and I just picked one
and went out to see them.

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:29.160
They were sort of on the
outskirts of Mexico city

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:31.420
in a very industrial area.

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:33.920
I started talking to the sales manager

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:36.467
and he basically said,

00:08:36.467 --> 00:08:38.970
"You can buy it as long
as you can pay for it."

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:42.260
He didn't require any proof
that I was a legitimate lab.

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:45.550
You know, you could easily
just walk in and buy this stuff

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:50.360
quite cheaply actually, and
take it to your heroin lab

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:53.000
and produce heroin with ease.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.106
So that was pretty shocking to see.

00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:01.940
In November 2019, I was in Mexico

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:03.140
reporting on the ground

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:05.490
and I went into this medical supply store

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:06.920
with a Mexican colleague

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:09.110
and we bought a one liter bottle,

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:12.400
glass bottle of JT Baker acetic anhydride.

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:14.080
And the seller volunteered to us

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:17.253
that he could easily
get us an 18 liter jug.

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:23.410
With that one 18 liter jug
that you can buy for about $300

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:26.530
you can make about a million
dollars worth of heroin.

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:30.470
And we also found that these
18 liter jugs were being sold

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:34.580
on the biggest e-commerce
platform in Latin America.

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:37.550
It's called Mercado Libre,
it's huge in Mexico.

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:40.540
It's kind of a mix
between Amazon and Alibaba

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:41.910
I guess you would say.

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:46.400
And it was on offer from
several sellers online publicly

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:47.950
in Mercado Libre.

00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:49.450
We weren't supposed to be able to buy it

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:51.250
unless we were legitimate buyers

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:52.773
but we didn't have any trouble getting it.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:55.840
One thing we noticed
on the Avantor products

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:57.257
that we were able to purchase is it said

00:09:57.257 --> 00:10:01.630
"Made in Mexico" in Spanish right there.

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:02.463
And we were like,

00:10:02.463 --> 00:10:04.850
well, that's interesting
because Avantor has, you know

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:07.590
these plants outside of
 the U.S. basically

00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:09.520
so how can they say 'Made in Mexico'?

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:12.680
And it turns out that
somehow they are bringing

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:17.610
the chemicals, the ingredients
and putting it into the jugs

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:20.440
in Mexico in a facility
they have in Mexico.

00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:24.770
And it's actually produced
by a subsidiary in Mexico.

00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:27.910
So it really is made in Mexico,
at least under Mexican law.

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:31.420
So that basically allows Avantor

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:35.160
and conceivably other
companies to produce this stuff

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:36.910
in Mexico which means they have to comply

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:38.273
with Mexican regulations.

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:41.610
Everything was done in Mexico

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:43.610
to create and sell this product.

00:10:43.610 --> 00:10:46.890
The company was able to
say that it did everything

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:49.720
perfectly legally under Mexican law

00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:52.170
'cause Mexican law was the
only thing that applied

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:55.730
'cause Mexico was kind of
this island unto itself

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:59.290
in international drug laws for
the heroin making chemical.

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:02.060
So they said of course, that
they hadn't violated the law

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:05.090
that their sellers, the
distributors and the retailers

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:09.373
that they sold to were responsible
for who the end user was.

00:11:10.606 --> 00:11:13.980
In 2014 alone, more
than 47,000 people died

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:17.290
from drug overdoses, more
than any single previous year

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:18.400
in American history.

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:20.680
In addition to cutting across

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:22.980
virtually every demographic in America

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:24.700
the heroin epidemic has cut across

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:26.940
virtually every region of the country.

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:32.300
No urban part of America
has been more devastated

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:36.220
by opioids, and by heroin,
than Philadelphia.

00:11:36.220 --> 00:11:39.560
The city of Philadelphia
has a large neighborhood

00:11:39.560 --> 00:11:40.800
called Kensington.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:43.870
It's an area that's become
synonymous with drug use.

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:47.180
It's even earned the nickname
"the Walmart of heroin".

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:49.340
The Drug Enforcement Administration

00:11:49.340 --> 00:11:53.820
routinely buys from undercover
buys and tests heroin

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:57.290
from across the United States
to do chemical analysis

00:11:57.290 --> 00:11:59.820
of where it's coming from
to determine its strength

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:01.650
its potency, its purity.

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:03.930
And they also track the
price because that gives them

00:12:03.930 --> 00:12:05.930
again, a good idea of what's happening.

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:09.830
The heroin that they've
bought in Philadelphia

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:12.200
which almost certainly
came from Kensington

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:16.720
is the most potent purist heroin
that they've found for sale

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:19.100
anywhere in the United States.

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:22.140
And the great irony of
that is that Avantor

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:24.780
which sells JT Baker
branded acetic anhydride

00:12:24.780 --> 00:12:27.290
that was used to make heroin in Mexico

00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:29.400
their headquarters is just 15 miles away

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:31.363
from the Kensington neighborhood.

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:35.580
The day that our story came out

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:39.440
Avantor, in consultation with its CEO

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.040
and its general counsel

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:43.860
decided immediately that they
were going to pull the product

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:45.630
from across Mexico.

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:49.100
It was a pretty extraordinary
move for them to make

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:51.350
and I think it was also quite telling

00:12:51.350 --> 00:12:54.300
in terms of how concerned they were

00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:59.830
with the evidence that we
published about how their product,

00:12:59.830 --> 00:13:04.010
and their company, was being used
to fuel heroin production

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:05.183
for the United States.

